KG42.register("rules-e632b727f3e13bf243159dbc",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R016","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R016","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The cost of supplying the generation deficit through imports from the retailer at the retail price should be covered. Scope: MMR treatment of a generation deficit within the energy sharing region at a time step. Condition: Total generation is less than total demand. Income from selling surplus generation to the retailer at the export price is to be distributed among all participants supplying electricity through generation or EV discharging. Scope: MMR distribution of income from surplus generation within the energy sharing region at a time step. Condition: Total generation is greater than total demand.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["settlement.payment"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"MMR distribution of income from surplus generation within the energy sharing region at a time step. | MMR treatment of a generation deficit within the energy sharing region at a time step.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-P01","symbol":"r_t^{retail}","meaning":"Retail price offered by the retailer agent at which the coordinator buys electricity for the energy sharing region (price per unit energy); fixed and pre-announced in the MMR setting, and used by the deficit-case settlement price formula (A26).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-P02","symbol":"r_t^{export}","meaning":"Export price offered by the retailer agent at which the coordinator sells electricity from the energy sharing region (price per unit energy); fixed and pre-announced in the MMR setting, and used by the surplus-case settlement price formula (A27).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-P03","symbol":"r_t^{average}","meaning":"Arithmetic mean of the retailer's export and retail prices, defined in the MMR pricing passage as r_t^{average} = (r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})/2; the reference price applied to locally balanced energy in the settlement price formulas.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"(r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})/2"},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-07"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The cost of supplying the generation deficit through imports from the retailer at the retail price should be covered. Scope: MMR treatment of a generation deficit within the energy sharing region at a time step. Condition: Total generation is less than total demand.","expression":"p_t^{buy} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\right) \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}}, \\qquad p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average}, \\qquad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \u003c \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-P01","v141-c-R016-P02","v141-c-R016-P03"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-07"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C002","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Income from selling surplus generation to the retailer at the export price is to be distributed among all participants supplying electricity through generation or EV discharging. Scope: MMR distribution of income from surplus generation within the energy sharing region at a time step. Condition: Total generation is greater than total demand.","expression":"p_t^{buy} = r_t^{average}, \\qquad p_t^{sell} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\right) \\cdot r_t^{export}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}|}, \\qquad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| > \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{PA}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-P01","v141-c-R016-P02","v141-c-R016-P03"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-07"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-07","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p26-c2r4__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":26,"printed_page":"1018","section":"A.2.2","anchor_text":"(A24) the internal price in diﬀerent ways according to the relationship between total n is equal to ","equation_id":"A25-A27","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-26.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"With the energy bids of all the prosumers, the coordinator calculates the internal price in different ways according to the relationship between total generation and demand in the energy sharing region. If the generation is equal to demand, the internal buying and selling price are equal, taking the average of the export and retail price:\n\np_t^{buy} = p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} = \\frac{(r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})}{2}, \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| = \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A25)\n\nIf the generation is less than demand, the deficit generation has to be supplied by the power imported from the retailer at the retail price, and the cost of this import should be covered. Therefore, in this situation, the internal selling price keeps the same as that in Formula (A25), but the buying price is modified:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \\right) \\cdot r_t^{retail}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{average} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| \u003c \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A26)\n\nSimilarly, if the generation is higher than demand, the surplus generation needs to be sold to the retailer at the export price, and this part of income needs to be distributed among all the prosumers who provide electricity by generation or EV discharging. The internal price is calculated as follows:\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{average} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = \\frac{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\cdot r_t^{average} + \\left( \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| - \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid} \\right) \\cdot r_t^{export}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}|} \\end{cases} \\quad \\text{if } \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{gen,n,t}^{bid}| > \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{dem,n,t}^{bid}.  (A27)\n\nFormulas (A25)-(A27) compose the pricing model in the coordinator agent under mid-market rate mechanism."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The settlement rule introduces no design-selection or operational decision variable. The decision variables of the underlying MMR model (appliance power and EV charging/discharging power x, determined in the prosumer decision-making model) and the resulting bid quantities e_gen,n,t^bid and e_dem,n,t^bid come from the bidding and pricing rules (bidding.supply, bidding.demand, pricing.local) and are not declared here; the internal prices p_t^buy and p_t^sell appearing in the transcribed settlement formulas are computed outcomes of the coordinator's pricing model, not free decisions, so they are not declared as x.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-07","quote":"If the generation is less than demand, the deficit generation has to be supplied by the power imported from the retailer at the retail price, and the cost of this import should be covered."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-07","quote":"Similarly, if the generation is higher than demand, the surplus generation needs to be sold to the retailer at the export price, and this part of income needs to be distributed among all the prosumers who provide electricity by generation or EV discharging."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"1876883944338ff0c8f787b0a4b5887868070cc63190b16e74f5039cbcf3e7f4","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Formalization of the MMR (v141-a-M02) settlement rule from the MMR price-formation passage on page 26 (Appendix A.2.2, evidence v141-b-g07-ev-07, an unreviewed candidate). C001 is formalized with the source case of Formula (A26): when sum_n |e_gen,n,t^bid| \u003c sum_n e_dem,n,t^bid, the internal buying price is set to the weighted average that charges local generation at r_t^average and the deficit imported from the retailer at r_t^retail, so that the deficit import cost is covered, while the internal selling price remains r_t^average. C002 is formalized with the source case of Formula (A27): when sum_n |e_gen,n,t^bid| > sum_n e_dem,n,t^bid, the internal selling price is set to the weighted average that remunerates local demand at r_t^average and the surplus exported to the retailer at r_t^export, so that the surplus export income is distributed among the participants supplying electricity by generation or EV discharging, while the buying price remains r_t^average. Signs, indices, sums over the region participant set PA and the inequality conditions are transcribed as printed, with generation magnitudes taken as absolute values and demand bids nonnegative; the time index t is retained. The equality branch (A25) is outside this rule's deficit/surplus scope and is therefore not duplicated here. Because the frozen graph contains only the node settlement.payment and no edges, the endogenous bid quantities and internal prices appearing in the transcribed formulas are neither decision variables x nor fixed inputs theta, so they were deliberately not declared as this rule's objects; only the retailer price parameters are declared. The two C.1 constraint entries are re-issued with unchanged constraint_id, statement, role, members and evidence_ids; only kind (procedural -> mathematical), expression, formalization_origin and parameter_refs were added. The evidence remains unreviewed: no independent source audit, no C2 review and no Agent E check were performed, so this transcription is provisional and must not be reported as source-verified.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is a settlement obligation of the approved function settlement.payment: in the deficit case the internal buying price of Formula (A26) (evidence v141-b-g07-ev-07) is defined so that the aggregate demand-side payment covers local generation valued at r_t^{average} plus the deficit imported from the retailer valued at r_t^{retail}. The frozen graph has E = [] and declares only settlement.payment, so no edge_id can be attached."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 is the settlement counterpart of the approved function settlement.payment: in the surplus case the internal selling price of Formula (A27) (evidence v141-b-g07-ev-07) is defined so that the aggregate income from local demand valued at r_t^{average} plus the exported surplus valued at r_t^{export} is distributed over the participants supplying generation/EV discharge. The frozen graph has E = [] and declares only settlement.payment, so no edge_id can be attached."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-P01","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"r_t^{retail} is a fixed, pre-announced retailer price (theta) entering the deficit-case settlement price formula (A26) attached to settlement.payment; the frozen graph for this rule has no edges, hence edge_ids is empty."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-P02","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"r_t^{export} is a fixed, pre-announced retailer price (theta) entering the surplus-case settlement price formula (A27) attached to settlement.payment; the frozen graph for this rule has no edges, hence edge_ids is empty."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-P03","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"r_t^{average} = (r_t^{export} + r_t^{retail})/2 is a derived constant used in both settlement price cases (A25)-(A27); declared as a symbolic parameter input to the two settlement constraints of settlement.payment. The frozen graph for this rule has no edges, hence edge_ids is empty."}],"revision_requests":["C.1 revision requested: the frozen graph for v141-c-R016 has V = [settlement.payment] and E = []. The settlement price formulas transcribed in C001/C002 take as inputs the aggregate MMR energy bids (sum_n |e_gen,n,t^bid| and sum_n e_dem,n,t^bid) and issue the internal prices p_t^buy and p_t^sell; add source-supported edges linking bidding.supply, bidding.demand and pricing.local to settlement.payment (same-mechanism evidence v141-b-g07-ev-07) so the settlement formulas' inputs and outputs are graph-representable.","Add typed objects (or cross-rule references with explicit source scope) for the endogenous quantities |e_gen,n,t^bid|, e_dem,n,t^bid, p_t^buy and p_t^sell: they are computed bid/price outcomes, so this rule deliberately did not declare them as x (decision variables) or theta (fixed inputs).","The paper provides no standalone settlement/payment equation distinct from the MMR price-formation formulas (A25)-(A27), which are also claimed by rule v141-c-R014 (pricing.local). If a separate settlement or cash-flow equation exists on pages not extracted for this rule, re-extract it; otherwise the settlement content of this rule is the deficit-coverage/surplus-distribution implication of the price formulas, as formalized here.","B evidence v141-b-g07-ev-07 is an unreviewed candidate (source_status = unverified). No independent source audit, no C2 review and no Agent E verification were performed in this experiment; the OCR of Formulas (A26) and (A27), including the absolute-value signs and inequality directions, should be re-verified before these transcriptions are treated as accepted source facts.","If the graph is to carry the settlement interpretation explicitly, C.1 should add a source-supported statement (or reference) that the equality case (A25) has no deficit/surplus and therefore lies outside this rule's scope, so that the two deficit/surplus branches remain the complete scope of settlement.payment for MMR."]},"C2_delivery":{"raw_sha256":"f78799810261976eceaf18fdf25965e642646ee90eb9c0b5b0fb31ef6e6bf712","delivery_payload_sha256":"25a65ba9660224a714f487d507a6aa94d73a8d88dbe634d280efe0c7213b7ac9","changes":[{"path":"theta.0.value.kind","before":"symbolic","after":"unspecified","reason":"Variant tag follows supplied value fields; no value, symbol or scientific statement is added, removed or rewritten."},{"path":"theta.1.value.kind","before":"symbolic","after":"unspecified","reason":"Variant tag follows supplied value fields; no value, symbol or scientific statement is added, removed or rewritten."}],"scientific_fields_unchanged":true,"request_graph_sha256":"1876883944338ff0c8f787b0a4b5887868070cc63190b16e74f5039cbcf3e7f4","scientific_correctness_verified":false}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
